<div class="hebrew-block">
וְהַלֵּוִי הוּא בְּחִינַת בִּינָה בְּחִינַת וְהָגוּת לִבִּי תְּבוּנוֹת. כִּי מִסִּטְרָא דִּלֵוִי דִּינִין מִתְעָרִין כְּמוּבָא בְּמָקוֹם אַחֵר. וְהַיִּשְׂרָאֵל הוּא בְּחִינַת הַשְּׁלִישִׁי הַמַּכְרִיעַ דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁהוּא מְקַשֵּׁר הַנְּקוּדָּה עִם הַוָּי״ו וְנַעֲשֶׂה בְּחִינַת מְלַאְפוּ״ם שֶׁשָּׁם הִתְגַּלּוּת הַנְּקוּדָּה כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב.
</div>

<p>
And the <em>Levi</em> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Binah</span> <span class="added">[Understanding]</span>, the aspect of <span class="verse">"and the meditation of my heart is understanding" <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 49:4)</span></span>. For from the side of <em>Levi</em>, judgments are aroused, as is brought elsewhere. And the <em>Yisra'ail</em> is the aspect of the <strong>third who decides</strong> — that is, he connects the <em>nekudah</em> with the <em>vav</em>, and it becomes the aspect of <em>melafum</em>, where the revelation of the <em>nekudah</em> occurs, as is written.
</p>

