כִּי עִקַּר הַבֵּית דִּין שֶׁעַל יָדוֹ נִיתָּר הַנֶּדֶר הוּא שְׁנַיִם. וְעַל כֵּן אֵין צְרִיכִין שֶׁיִּהְיוּ כֻּלָּם גְּמִירֵי רַק ב' מֵהֶם כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב בַּשֻּׁלְחָן עָרוּךְ. רַק שֶׁהַשְּׁלִישִׁי בָּא לְהַכְרִיעַ שֶׁלֹּא יְהֵי בֵּית דִּין חָלוּק כְּמוֹ דְּאִיתָא בְּסַנְהֶדְרִין לְעִנְיַן דַּיָּנִים. כִּי אִם לֹא יִהְיֶה רַק ב' אֶפְשָׁר שֶׁיִּתְחַלְּקוּ חַס וְשָׁלוֹם וְלֹא יְהִי הִתְקַשְּׁרוּת הַוָּי״ו אֶל הַנְּקוּדָּה מֵאַחַר שֶׁהֵם בְּחִינוֹת שׁוֹנוֹת עַל כֵּן בָּא הַשְּׁלִישִׁי לְהַכְרִיעַ וְעַל יָדוֹ נִתְקַשְּׁרִים יַחַד הַוָּי״ו אֶל הַנְּקוּדָּה וְנַעֲשֶׂה בְּחִינַת מְלַאְפוּ״ם בְּחִינַת הַרְחֵב פִּיךָ וַאֲמַלְאֵהוּ שֶׁעַל יְדֵי זֶה יֵשׁ לָהֶם מֶמְשָׁלָה כַּנַּ״ל וּכְמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב שָׁם בַּמַּאֲמָר הַנַּ״ל עַיֵּן שָׁם:
</div>

<p>
For the primary <em>bais din</em> through which the vow is annulled consists of two <span class="added">[judges]</span>. Therefore they do not all need to be <span class="key-term">gemiray</span> <span class="added">[learned in Torah law]</span> — only two of them, as is written in the <em>Shulchan Aruch</em>. Rather, the third comes to decide, so that the <em>bais din</em> should not be divided, as it is found in <span class="added">[Tractate]</span> Sanhedrin regarding judges. For if there were only two, it is possible that they would be divided, G-d forbid, and there would be no connection of the <em>vav</em> to the <em>nekudah</em>, since they are different aspects. Therefore the third comes to decide, and through him the <em>vav</em> and the <em>nekudah</em> are bound together, becoming the aspect of <em>melafum</em>, the aspect of <span class="verse">"Open your mouth wide and I will fill it" <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 81:11)</span></span> — through which they have dominion, as mentioned above, and as is written there in the aforementioned discourse; see there.
</p>

