וְזֶה בְּחִינַת יָחִיד מוּמְחֶה שֶׁמַּתִּיר הַנֶּדֶר בְּיָחִיד כִּי אֵצֶל הַתַּלְמִיד חָכָם וְהַמּוּמְחֶה שָׁם הוּא בְּחִינַת נְקוּדָּה כְּלָלִיּוּת יִשְׂרָאֵל כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב שָׁם וְעַל כֵּן יֵשׁ בּוֹ מֶמְשָׁלָה לְהַתִּיר הַנֶּדֶר שֶׁאָסַר הַיִּשְׂרְאֵלִי עַל עַצְמוֹ עַל יְדֵי דִּבּוּר פִּיו כַּנַּ״ל. כִּי עַתָּה נִתְגַּלָּה אוֹר חָדָשׁ שֶׁהוּא גָּדוֹל בְּיוֹתֵר דְּהַיְנוּ בְּחִינַת נְקוּדָּה כְּלָלִיּוּת שֶׁהוּא אֵצֶל הַתַּלְמִיד חָכָם שֶׁבַּדּוֹר. אוֹ עַל יְדֵי הַנְּקוּדָּה כְּלָלִיּוּת שֶׁנִּתְגַּלָּה עַל יְדֵי ג' אֲנָשִׁים כַּנַּ״ל:
</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <strong>an individual expert</strong> (<span class="key-term">yachid mumcheh</span>) who annuls the vow by himself alone. For in the presence of the <span class="key-term">talmid chacham</span> <span class="added">[Torah scholar]</span> and expert, there is the aspect of the <em>nekudah</em> of the totality of Israel, as is written there. Therefore he has the dominion to annul the vow that the Jew forbade upon himself through the speech of his mouth, as mentioned above. For now a new light has been revealed, which is exceedingly great — namely, the aspect of the all-encompassing <em>nekudah</em>, which is found with the <em>talmid chacham</em> of the generation. Or <span class="added">[alternatively, the annulment takes place]</span> through the all-encompassing <em>nekudah</em> that is revealed through three men, as mentioned above.
</p>

