<p>
And he must have <span class="key-term">charatah</span> <span class="added">[regret]</span>, which is an aspect of <em>sheviras halev</em> <span class="added">[brokenheartedness]</span>, and he must bring the regret before those who annul <span class="added">[the vow]</span> — that is, he declares before them that he regrets. And they rectify the brokenheartedness through the <em>nekudah</em> that is in their mouths, which is the aspect of "a <em>tzadik</em> rules," and they say to him, <strong>"It is permitted to you"</strong> (<em>mutar lach</em>). And through this, it returns to a state of being permitted, as mentioned above.
